bowshock is an independent implementation of published numerical methods.
It contains no code from FluidX3D.

Methods implemented, with references, are listed below and cited at the
point of use in the source code.

Shock tube test problem
  G. A. Sod, "A survey of several finite difference methods for systems of
  nonlinear hyperbolic conservation laws", J. Comput. Phys. 27, 1978.

Exact Riemann solver for the Euler equations
  E. F. Toro, Riemann Solvers and Numerical Methods for Fluid Dynamics,
  3rd ed., Springer, 2009, chapter 4 (also the source of the five 1D test
  problems in src/validation/toro-tests.ts).

HLLC approximate Riemann solver
  E. F. Toro, M. Spruce and W. Speares, "Restoration of the contact surface
  in the HLL-Riemann solver", Shock Waves 4, 1994.
  P. Batten, N. Clarke, C. Lambert and D. M. Causon, "On the choice of
  wavespeeds for the HLLC Riemann solver", SIAM J. Sci. Comput. 18(6), 1997.

Wave-speed estimates
  B. Einfeldt, "On Godunov-type methods for gas dynamics", SIAM J. Numer.
  Anal. 25(2), 1988.

MUSCL reconstruction and slope limiters
  B. van Leer, "Towards the ultimate conservative difference scheme. II.
  Monotonicity and conservation combined in a second-order scheme",
  J. Comput. Phys. 14, 1974 (harmonic limiter).
  B. van Leer, "Towards the ultimate conservative difference scheme. IV.
  A new approach to numerical convection", J. Comput. Phys. 23, 1977
  (monotonized central limiter).
  B. van Leer, "Towards the ultimate conservative difference scheme. V.
  A second-order sequel to Godunov's method", J. Comput. Phys. 32, 1979.
  G. D. van Albada, B. van Leer and W. W. Roberts, "A comparative study of
  computational methods in cosmic gas dynamics", Astron. Astrophys. 108, 1982.

Strong-stability-preserving Runge-Kutta time integration
  C.-W. Shu and S. Osher, "Efficient implementation of essentially
  non-oscillatory shock-capturing schemes", J. Comput. Phys. 77, 1988.

Compensated summation of the GPU clock (TwoSum)
  D. E. Knuth, The Art of Computer Programming, vol. 2: Seminumerical
  Algorithms, Addison-Wesley.

Isentropic vortex verification case
  C.-W. Shu, "Essentially non-oscillatory and weighted essentially
  non-oscillatory schemes for hyperbolic conservation laws", in Advanced
  Numerical Approximation of Nonlinear Hyperbolic Equations, Lecture Notes
  in Mathematics 1697, Springer, 1998.

Oblique shock, normal shock and Prandtl-Meyer relations
  Ames Research Staff, "Equations, Tables, and Charts for Compressible
  Flow", NACA Report 1135, 1953.


Nose cone profiles (src/geometry/nose.ts)
  Shapes and parameter conventions as defined by OpenRocket
  (core/src/main/java/info/openrocket/core/rocketcomponent/Transition.java,
  https://github.com/openrocket/openrocket), so that imported designs
  match; the formulas are reimplemented, no OpenRocket code is included.
  Haack series: W. Haack, "Geschossformen kleinsten Wellenwiderstandes",
  Bericht 139 der Lilienthal-Gesellschaft fuer Luftfahrtforschung, 1941.
  The tests check its defining slender-body property directly.
